      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T23:07:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is sort of subtle as you are making the sha be {0x0, 0xff, ... , 0xff }.  And computing the sha of the { 0xff..0xff } buffer (including layout_version, padding, reserved, etc). If you just cycle through a few generation numbers you\u0027d get the same thing -- but more explicitly after setting the metadata inline with expectations. Something to think about. right now everything is 0xff\u0027s except sha, generation, and layout_version.\n\nOn that note, you end up with both slots occupied with the same generation number once you are done w/ this loop.",
      "revId": "94a5f82c78f9bf65262025e68de721a60af32371",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
